# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The NetSuite private key and the Anthropic API key both live OUTSIDE this
# folder (%USERPROFILE%\.po-agent\), so they are not at risk here. These
# patterns are defence in depth in case one is ever generated in-tree.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.key
*.cer
*.crt
*.der
*.jks
*.keystore
credentials
credentials.json

# Real vendor documents containing banking or third-party commercial data live
# outside the project at %USERPROFILE%\.po-agent\vendor-documents-private\ — see
# RUNBOOK §6 item 1. Scoped to the project root: fixtures/ holds the SYNTHETIC
# stand-in, which the attachment-classifier tests need and which contains no
# real banking details.
#
# These patterns are a net for the NEXT arrival, not a fix for the files already
# moved (those never reached a commit). A vendor document SET routinely attaches
# an invoice, a payment request and a bill of lading alongside the packing list,
# and those carry bank accounts, SWIFT codes, MID codes and other customers'
# names even when the packing list itself is clean. So the invoice-shaped members
# of a set are ignored by default and admitted only deliberately.
/*Payment Request*.pdf
/*COMMERCIAL INVOICE*.xls
/*COMMERCIAL INVOICE*.xlsx
/*Clearance Invoice*.xls
/*Clearance Invoice*.xlsx
/*Payment invoice*.xls
/*Payment invoice*.xlsx
/*HBL*.pdf
/*BILL OF LADING*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated / transient output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The local development database. Built from migration 0001 -- never committed,
# because the schema lives in the migration and the DATA in it would be real
# vendor and PO information.
po_agent.db
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite3

# parse_packing_slip.py's default CSV output, and ad-hoc extraction dumps.
proposed_updates.csv
*.tmp.xlsx
vendor_results/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
# Office lock files — OneDrive folders collect these whenever a doc is open.
~$*
